# S9 acceptance transcript: Meta definitions rewritten.
#
# S8 |- S9. What a meaning is becomes Strata's.
#
# S8 moved what a syntax is. This moves the other half. Meta elaboration is
# not the same kind of function: it invents declarations nobody wrote -- a
# constructor and a predicate per variant for every `data`, a constructor and
# an accessor per field for every `record` -- each named by concatenating onto
# the type's name. That is why a name is text here rather than carried
# unopened, and it is the whole difference between this layer and the last.
#
# Forty-three Meta sources, byte for byte, replayed by the first line.

